; The EXT connector, on the right edge under the volume dial, where a DMG keeps
; it behind a little door.
;
; +Z points OUT of the shell, the convention every port in the room follows, so
; this one is turned a quarter turn about Y to look along +X. 1 mm proud of the
; panel: a seated link plug's origin is the front face of its shell, and that
; face stops almost flush against the socket's rim.
;
; A .tscn lists a basis by ROWS, not by the columns the Transform3D constructor
; takes, so a quarter turn written from the columns comes out as its own
; transpose -- which for a rotation is its inverse. That put +Z along -X, into
; the shell, and the lead left the plug through the console and had to climb back
; over the screen. Copy this basis from the junction's own LinkPort, which faces
; +X too; do NOT copy it from the GBA's, whose matrix is symmetric and reads the
; same under either convention.
[node name="LinkPort" parent="." instance=ExtResource("9_linkport")]
transform = Transform3D(0, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, -1, 0, 0, 0.0437, 0, 0.008)
